layout: layouts/base.njk
metaTitle: "FAQ | What to Expect | Laguna Beach Counseling"
description: "What a first session is like, whether you take insurance, how Beach Therapy works, and what happens if therapy didn't help before."
permalink: /faq/
crumbs:
  - { label: "Home", url: "/" }
  - { label: "FAQ" }
---
{# /faq, a CUSTOM page (no page template): the canonical answer-engine hub. It
   presents the ENTIRE faq.json answer engine (every entry) in one place, organized
   into logical category accordions, and emits the ONE canonical FAQPage schema over
   all of them. Every other page's FAQ pulls a small tag-subset of the same faq.json
   and emits its own (subset) FAQPage; /get-started deliberately emits none, so this
   page is the single complete FAQPage. Duplication of a question across different
   page URLs is expected and fine; each page's FAQPage validly describes its own
   visible Q&A.

   The category buckets are built by auto-partitioning faqEntries: each entry is
   placed in the FIRST category (in the order below) whose tags intersect the entry's
   tags, and never twice (placedIds guard), so no question repeats across categories
   or in the schema. A catch-all sweeps up any entry whose tags match no category, so
   future faq.json additions can never silently vanish from this page. Accumulation
   uses the Nunjucks array-mutation pattern (.push on arrays declared in an outer
   scope), since Nunjucks {% set %} inside a loop does not otherwise persist.

   Brief internal links: /fees and /beach-therapy (intro) and /get-started (CTA), all
   real. H1/title/meta match the brief exactly. One gold CTA (the closing band). No
   em dashes. #}
{% import "components/ui.njk" as ui %}
{% import "components/sections.njk" as s %}

{{ s.breadcrumbs(crumbs) }}

{{ s.hero({
  eyebrow: "FAQ",
  title: "Questions people ask before",
  titleEmphasis: "reaching out.",
  variant: "center",
  lead: "The honest answers to what people wonder before they pick up the phone. If yours isn't here, the free call is the best place to ask it.",
  cta: { href: site.booking.getStartedPath, label: site.booking.navLabel }
}) }}

{% call s.prose({ width: "narrow" }) %}
  <p>A couple of the big ones have pages of their own: what therapy actually costs lives on the <a href="/fees">fees page</a>, and how walk-and-talk sessions work is all on the <a href="/beach-therapy">Beach Therapy</a> page. Everything else is right here, grouped so you can find your question fast.</p>
{% endcall %}

{% set cats = [
  { title: "Getting started", eyebrow: "First things first", tags: ["getting-started"] },
  { title: "Cost and insurance", eyebrow: "The money question", tags: ["cost"] },
  { title: "Telehealth", eyebrow: "Therapy by video", tags: ["telehealth"] },
  { title: "Beach Therapy", eyebrow: "Our signature service", tags: ["beach-therapy"] },
  { title: "Couples and relationships", eyebrow: "When there are two of you", tags: ["couples", "infidelity"] },
  { title: "Families, teens, and children", eyebrow: "The whole family", tags: ["families", "teens", "children", "mother-daughter"] },
  { title: "Seniors and later life", eyebrow: "The later chapters", tags: ["seniors", "grief"] },
  { title: "Anxiety and depression", eyebrow: "When it feels heavy", tags: ["anxiety", "depression"] },
  { title: "More about the work", eyebrow: "Everything else", tags: ["life-transitions", "neurodiversity", "faith", "medication", "general"] }
] %}

{# rendered holds only the categories that actually produce questions, so the jump
   index below is built from the same pass that builds the sections. A category that
   empties out (Beach Therapy is empty today: all four of its entries are blocked)
   disappears from both, and a new one appears in both, with no second list to keep
   in sync by hand. #}
{% set allItems = [] %}
{% set placedIds = [] %}
{% set rendered = [] %}
{% for cat in cats %}
  {% set catItems = [] %}
  {% for e in faqEntries %}{% if not e.blocked %}
    {% if e.id not in placedIds %}
      {% set matches = [] %}
      {% for t in cat.tags %}{% if t in e.tags %}{% set _ = matches.push(1) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {% if matches | length %}
        {% set _ = catItems.push({ q: e.question, a: e.answer }) %}
        {% set _ = allItems.push({ q: e.question, a: e.answer }) %}
        {% set _ = placedIds.push(e.id) %}
      {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  {% if catItems | length %}
    {% set _ = rendered.push({ title: cat.title, eyebrow: cat.eyebrow, items: catItems, slug: cat.title | slugify }) %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{# Catch-all: any entry whose tags matched no category above, so nothing is dropped. #}
{% set restItems = [] %}
{% set restEntries = [] %}
{% for e in faqEntries %}{% if not e.blocked %}
  {% if e.id not in placedIds %}
    {% set _ = restItems.push({ q: e.question, a: e.answer }) %}
    {% set _ = restEntries.push(e) %}
    {% set _ = allItems.push({ q: e.question, a: e.answer }) %}
    {% set _ = placedIds.push(e.id) %}
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{# Build-time guard: warns when the catch-all grows past the size of the smallest
   deliberately named category, which is the point it stops being a remainder. It
   is handed the real orphans from this very loop, so the check cannot drift from
   the partition. Renders nothing and never fails the build. #}
{{ restEntries | warnOnCatchAll }}
{% if restItems | length %}
  {% set _ = rendered.push({ title: "Other questions", eyebrow: "One more thing", items: restItems, slug: "Other questions" | slugify }) %}
{% endif %}

{# The jump index, then the sections. Both loop over `rendered`, so the links and the
   targets cannot drift apart. pillLinks fits as-is: it already takes {href,label},
   has the centered variant, renders real anchors (so tab order is document order and
   .pill-links__pill:focus-visible already styles the focus ring), and needs no JS.
   No smooth scroll: nothing in the CSS sets scroll-behavior, so these are instant
   jumps, which is both the motion-safe choice and the better one here. #}
{% set indexLinks = [] %}
{% for r in rendered %}{% set _ = indexLinks.push({ href: "#" + r.slug, label: r.title }) %}{% endfor %}
{{ s.pillLinks({
  id: "all-questions",
  eyebrow: "Jump to",
  title: "Find your question",
  align: "center",
  tone: "sand",
  links: indexLinks
}) }}

{% for r in rendered %}
  {{ s.faq({
    id: r.slug,
    eyebrow: r.eyebrow,
    title: r.title,
    items: r.items,
    backLink: { href: "#all-questions", label: "Back to all questions" }
  }) }}
{% endfor %}

{{ s.ctaBand({
  variant: "center",
  tone: "sand",
  watermark: "Curious",
  title: "Still wondering about something?",
  text: "The best answers come from an actual conversation. A free 15 to 20 minute call is a no-pressure way to ask us anything at all.",
  tagline: site.tagline,
  cta: { href: site.booking.getStartedPath, label: site.booking.navLabel }
}) }}

{# The single canonical FAQPage schema over every entry, each exactly once, in the
   same order they appear above. #}
{{ s.faqSchema(allItems) }}
{{ s.breadcrumbSchema(crumbs, site.url) }}
